  "canonicalization_profile": "keel.canonical_json.payload.v1",
  "conformance": "Passing every vector is NECESSARY, NOT SUFFICIENT for conformance. The ruleset's decision_algorithm plus the profile/grammar definitions are the complete contract; this corpus is mandatory minimum evidence. Each vector's `given.available_artifacts` fixes the verifier's dependency-resolution state so resolution outcomes are deterministic and not environment-dependent.",
  "digest_consistency": "Every vector whose facts carry a registry artifact_digest equal to this header classification_registry_digest MUST also, when resolved against a store containing the pinned registry, agree with it. A vector that references a different digest MUST supply the matching `given` store or expect unverifiable. Header and vector digests disagreeing without an explicit store override invalidates this corpus artifact; it never silently changes a vector's expected outcome.",
  "outcomes": [
    "valid",
    "no_derivation",
    "invalid",
    "unverifiable"
  ],
  "deferred_coverage": "multiple-applicable-rules (needs a synthetic 2-rule fixture; lands with the second Permit-to-X rule), artifact-bytes-hash-mismatch corruption case, and property/generated tests are broader-assurance, co-designed with the reference verifier. Enumerated here so their absence is explicit, not silent.",
